summary is: {{ HPC: 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, presents with left elbow pain. 

O/E: Left elbow pain, erythema and edema, pain with palpation, warm to palpation. No swelling, no weakness, no numbness, no tingling. No fever, no chills. 

Imp: Olecranon bursitis. 

Plan: Meloxicam 15mg OD, rest, ice. 

HPC: Continue keppra 500mg BD. 

HPC: Continue lexapro 10mg OD. 

HPC: Continue protonix 40mg OD before meals. 

Imp: All other systems normal. 

Imp: No abnormality on xray of left elbow. 

Imp: Endoscopy: gastritis. 

Plan: Review in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
