summary is: {{ HPC: 49 year old male with resistant hypertension, palpitations, and a history of hypertension since young age. He has been taking Benicar HCT and amlodipine, but his blood pressure has not been controlled. He has been drinking less salt and trying to walk regularly. He has a family history of hypertension. He has been taking potassium 4.0. He has been having blood pressure around 146-155 in the morning. His blood pressure has not been controlled on three medications.

Impression: Resistant hypertension.

Plan: Add spironolactone to his regimen. He will need to have a metabolic panel and blood pressure check in two weeks. He will need to monitor his potassium and sodium levels. He will need to hydrate regularly and report any dizziness. He will need to report any breast tenderness or swelling. He will need to monitor his blood pressure regularly. He will need to have a follow up in two weeks to check his blood pressure and electrolytes. If his blood pressure is not controlled, he will need to go to the resistant hypertension clinic. He will need to look at the dash eating plan and try to lower his salt intake. He will need to do exercise regularly. He will need to monitor his blood pressure regularly. He will need to have a follow up in two weeks to check his blood pressure and electrolytes. }}<|eot_id|>
