summary is: {{ Hx: 20-year-old female, presents with symptoms of discomfort, change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She has been having sexual encounters with her partner, who recently revealed that he has been having multiple partners. She reports right-sided vaginal pain. 
Imp: Normal physical exam, normal labia, no external lesions, normal physiological discharge. No cervical motion tenderness, no adnexal tenderness or masses noted. Swabs were done for std testing. 
Plan: std testing for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, and blood testing for syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c. Will call her in 3 days for results. If normal, will see her at her next annual checkup. }}<|eot_id|>
