summary is: {{ HPC: 57-year-old male with a 2-week history of shortness of breath, coughing up blood and sputum. PMHx: DM, HTN, asthma. 
Imp: CXR: WNL. PE: Temp: 37.2, BP: 120/70, HR: 70, RR: 20, O2 sat: 94% on room air. Lungs: RR: 20, rhonchi on RLL, diminished breath sounds on RLL. HE: RRR, no murmurs. Abdo: soft and non-tender. Ext: 1+ pedal edema. 
Plan: 
- CXR
- CT chest
- Blood work
- Referral to ED
- Hold Norvasc for now
- Increase Metformin to 750mg BD
- Review in 3 weeks for DM
- Hold Norvasc for now until shortness of breath is under control }}<|eot_id|>
