summary is: {{ HPC: 1: Subjective: 
Patient is a 68 year old female who has had a nonhealing foot ulcer for one year. She has type 2 diabetes and has been on antibiotics for 5 months. She has been having some drainage and has been feeling a little bit tired lately. She has been walking around on the ulcer. She is currently on metformin and insulin. She has an a1c of 10. She is planning on walking around at the zoo this weekend. 
HPC: 2: Objective: 
On examination, the patient has a 1x2 cm ulcer on the dorsal aspect of the lateral right foot. There is some yellow slough present with minimal granulation tissue. There is no surrounding erythema or cellulitis. There is no fluid collection and no necrosis. The patient does not have any pain when the area is touched. 
HPC: 3: Assessment: 
Impression: nonhealing foot ulcer. 
Impression: nonhealing foot ulcer. 
HPC: 4: Plan: 
Imp: 1: Debridement of the ulcer 
Imp: 2: Prescribe colaganase ointment 
Imp: 3: Get a surgical shoe 
Imp: 4: Follow up in 2 weeks for another debridement and to check the ulcer. 
Imp: 5: Continue to monitor blood sugar levels and to follow up with primary care provider about the a1c. }}<|eot_id|>
