summary is: {{ HPC: 82-year-old male with a past medical history of hypertension and stage three chronic kidney disease who presents for hospital follow-up after an acute on chronic CHF exacerbation. He reports that his ankles have been swelling and he has been short of breath for the past few days. He has been having high blood pressure and has been in the hospital for the past few days. He was treated with bumex 2mg daily and has been instructed to continue his medications and watch his diet. He has been instructed to weigh himself daily and to call if he gains 3 pounds in 2 days. He has been instructed to see a nutritionist to receive education on diet. He is to continue on cozaar 100mg daily and norvasc 5mg daily. He has been instructed to have a renal artery ultrasound. He has been instructed to have more blood work to ensure that he is tolerating his regimen. }}<|eot_id|>
