summary is: {{ PC: 45 yr male, presented with right ankle pain and swelling after falling on the ice. 
Hx: 
- Fell on the ice and was unable to walk on it initially
- Currently has a limp
- Has been using ice and ibuprofen, which has helped
- No numbness or tingling in the foot
- No history of ankle injuries in the past
- Plays soccer regularly

Imp: Right ankle sprain
Plan: 
- Continue to elevate the leg and use ice
- Use crutches for 1-2 days
- May start walking on it as tolerated
- Follow up in 2 weeks to assess progress
- Use NSAIDs as needed for pain
- May need to be off soccer for 2 weeks
- May need to use aircast for 1-2 weeks
- May need to be off work for 1-2 weeks
