summary is: {{ HPC: 6/10
Hx: 6 months of knee pain, deep achy pain, worse with standing, stairs, getting up from seated position. Pain improves with rest. No specific event. No swelling, redness. No trauma. No fever. No nausea/vomiting/diarrhea. No history of trauma. No previous knee problems.
Imp: Bilateral patellofemoral pain syndrome.
Exam: Normal gait. Normal strength 5/5 in lower extremities. Normal reflexes. Normal patella and achilles reflexes. No swelling, redness, or effusion. Tenderness to palpation of retinacular retinaculum. Positive patellar grind test. Lachman, anterior and posterior drawer, and McMurray tests all negative.
Imp: Bilateral patellofemoral pain syndrome.
Plan: Ibuprofen/anti-inflammatory as needed. Physical therapy to increase strength, mobility, and correct running mechanics. Take it easy from running for now. Follow-up soon. }}<|eot_id|>
